Campfire wasm patch 0108: the address-expiry check does not re-enter itself.

NotificationCenter::checkAddressesExpirationTime() creates a notification
for every expired address. Creating one notifies the subscribers;
WalletClient's subscriber recounts the unread notifications
(updateNotifications -> getUnreadCount -> getNotifications), and
getNotifications() runs checkAddressesExpirationTime() again, which creates
the next notification. So the call nests one level (about ten frames) per
expired address. A wallet with a long history - many addresses, long
expired - ran out of stack on the web wallet's wallet thread (a browser
worker): "RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded" at start, the wallet
thread died, nothing ever answered and the app moved between nodes forever.
Native builds have a much larger stack and survive it.

With this, a call made while one is already running returns at once. The
outer pass still walks every address and creates every notification; the
nested recount sees the notifications made so far, and the outer pass
finishes the rest. Found by importing such a wallet.db (2026-10-10).

--- a/wallet/client/extensions/notifications/notification_center.h
+++ b/wallet/client/extensions/notifications/notification_center.h
@@ -70,5 +70,6 @@
 
         std::vector<WalletAddress> m_myAddresses;
         io::Timer::Ptr m_checkoutTimer;
+        bool m_checkingExpiration = false; // Campfire (wasm patch 0108)
     };
 } // namespace beam::wallet
